WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.000
Align an eight-bit addition
00000111; + 00000001
Both operands are unsigned. Start adding in the rightmost column.

2
00:00:04.000 --> 00:00:08.000
Carry from the right
Binary 1 + 1 = 10; Write 0; carry 1
The carried 1 continues through the next two columns containing 1s.

3
00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:12.000
Read the complete sum
00000111 + 00000001; Result: 00001000; Denary check: 7 + 1 = 8
The result fits in the available eight bits.

4
00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:16.000
Shift the result left once
00001000 -&gt; 00010000; Denary: 8 -&gt; 16
A zero enters on the right. No significant bit is lost, so the value doubles.

5
00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:20.000
Start again and shift right
Start again: 00001000; Right shift: 00000100; Denary: 8 -&gt; 4
This separate check starts from 8 again. A zero enters on the left.

6
00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:24.000
Check an addition that is too large
11111111 + 00000001; Full sum: 1 00000000; 256 &gt; 255: unsigned overflow
The complete result needs nine bits. Keeping only eight would lose its value.
